# First-stage fstab for the Hisense A9 mainline-kernel Android boot (DRAFT 2026-10-15).
# Lives in the boot ramdisk root as /fstab.hlte556n. Found by the stock A11
# first-stage init via GetFstabPath(): androidboot.fstab_suffix, then
# androidboot.hardware, then hardware.platform, prefixes /odm/etc/fstab.,
# /vendor/etc/fstab., /fstab. (system/core android-11.0.0_r48
# fs_mgr/fs_mgr_fstab.cpp:408). Our header cmdline sets fstab_suffix=hlte556n
# BEFORE the ABL's own "androidboot.fstab_suffix=default"; the first occurrence
# wins (fs_mgr_boot_config.cpp fs_mgr_get_boot_config_from_kernel).
#
# Rules (see the report):
#  - ONLY the two logical partitions system and vendor of slot _b
#    (androidboot.slot_suffix=_b is pinned on our cmdline, first occurrence wins).
#  - read-only; super metadata marks both "readonly" (lpdump of the golden
#    super.bin, MEASURED), so fs_mgr loads the dm-linear tables read-only
#    (fs_mgr_dm_linear.cpp:124) and dm opens super without write access.
#  - no avb / avb_keys (AVB is off on this phone), no "check" (no e2fsck run),
#    no "discard", no "formattable".
#  - NOTHING else: no userdata, metadata, misc, persist, modem, dsp, bluetooth,
#    SD card. product/system_ext are NOT mounted: the GSI's own
#    /system/product and /system/system_ext are used (root symlinks), unlike
#    today's stock fstab which overmounts stock A11 product_b/system_ext_b.
#
#<src>  <mnt_point>  <type>  <mnt_flags>          <fs_mgr_flags>
system  /system      ext4    ro,barrier=1         wait,slotselect,logical,first_stage_mount
vendor  /vendor      ext4    ro,barrier=1         wait,slotselect,logical,first_stage_mount
